Vendored Wayland protocol definitions.

Copied verbatim from the upstream packages, kept here so the module builds from
its own directory without a system wayland-protocols, and so the version the
bindings were generated from is pinned rather than whatever the build host has.
Each file keeps its own upstream copyright header.

  wayland.xml                          wayland 1.26.0        /usr/share/wayland/
  xdg-shell.xml                        wayland-protocols 1.49  stable/xdg-shell/
  viewporter.xml                       wayland-protocols 1.49  stable/viewporter/
  cursor-shape-v1.xml                  wayland-protocols 1.49  staging/cursor-shape/
  fractional-scale-v1.xml              wayland-protocols 1.49  staging/fractional-scale/
  xdg-decoration-unstable-v1.xml       wayland-protocols 1.49  unstable/xdg-decoration/
  pointer-constraints-unstable-v1.xml  wayland-protocols 1.49  unstable/pointer-constraints/
  relative-pointer-unstable-v1.xml     wayland-protocols 1.49  unstable/relative-pointer/

Re-check against the host packages with:

  pkg-config --modversion wayland-client wayland-protocols
  md5sum protocols/*.xml
  md5sum /usr/share/wayland/wayland.xml \
         /usr/share/wayland-protocols/stable/{xdg-shell/xdg-shell,viewporter/viewporter}.xml \
         /usr/share/wayland-protocols/staging/{cursor-shape/cursor-shape-v1,fractional-scale/fractional-scale-v1}.xml \
         /usr/share/wayland-protocols/unstable/{xdg-decoration/xdg-decoration-unstable-v1,pointer-constraints/pointer-constraints-unstable-v1,relative-pointer/relative-pointer-unstable-v1}.xml

wayland.xml is vendored for its interface definitions only. Its tables are
already compiled into libwayland-client, so the generator emits `extern`
declarations for the core interfaces and a table for nothing in that file.
